  "readmeFile": "Readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.1.0\n\nInitial public SerilogRelay package.\n\n- Targets .NET 8 and .NET 10.\n- Adds the Serilog `.WriteTo.SerilogRelay(...)` sink for HTTP log delivery.\n- Persists events to a bounded local SQLite application spool before normal network delivery.\n- Reuses stable `EventId` values across retries and restarts while using `BatchId` for delivery-attempt correlation.\n- Supports shared application spools across multiple processes with atomic short-lived delivery claims and takeover after process failure.\n- Allows surviving or newer processes to drain backlog created by another process of the same application.\n- Provides configurable sent retention, optional unsent maximum age, and physical spool-size limits.\n- Adds process-local exponential endpoint retry with jitter and optional HTTP `Retry-After` handling.\n- Adds a bounded emergency memory buffer for temporary local persistence failures.\n- Adds SQLite corruption quarantine/recovery and recreates the spool when corruption is detected.\n- Uses normal platform TLS certificate validation by default; accepting any server certificate requires an explicit dangerous opt-in.\n- Supports an optional opaque bearer token sent as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.\n- Includes `ApplicationId`, `MachineId`, and `ProcessId` producer metadata in the relay payload.\n- Uses at-least-once HTTP delivery semantics: non-2xx/transport failures remain pending for later retry or takeover.\n- Keeps receiver persistence, duplicate presentation, and server-side storage policy outside the sink contract.",
